tery A because it has a non-empty set of probable outcomes with an average of -4000, while Lottery B has no probable outcomes. So the reason would lead to choosing Lottery A. The information required by the reason (probabilities and outcomes) is fully available from the lotteries, and the rule can be applied. The reason is applicable.",
